== Economy ==

Oita Prefecture's economy is driven by small-ship building, maritime logistics, and ocean fishing. The prefecture's GDP was approximately 円14 billion in 2025, with industry (shipbuilding and fish processing) accounting for 40%, services 35%, and agriculture/fisheries 25%.

=== Small-ship building ===
[[File:Oita Shipbuilding District.jpg|thumb|left|250px|The Oita Shipbuilding District, Okaiken's primary centre for small-to-medium vessel construction]]
The {{nihongo|Oita Shipbuilding District|大分造船地区|Oita Zōsen Chiku}}, stretching along the northern coast of Oita Island, is Okaiken's primary centre for small-to-medium vessel construction. The district houses approximately 30 shipyards, producing fishing vessels (20–80 metres), coasters, ferry craft, tugs, and patrol vessels. The district's annual output is approximately 120 vessels, with a combined tonnage of approximately 180,000 GT.

The {{nihongo|Oita Shipwrights' Guild|大分船大工組合|Oita Funadaiku Kumiai}}, which traces its origins to 1452, oversees apprenticeship programmes and quality standards. The Guild has successfully integrated traditional wooden boat-building techniques with modern steel and composite construction, producing vessels that are noted for their seaworthiness in the heavy seas of the southeastern Shendan. The shipbuilding sector employs approximately 6,500 workers and generates approximately 円6 billion in annual revenue.

=== Maritime logistics ===
The [[Port of Oita]] is the primary resupply hub for the southeastern Shendan Ocean, providing fuel, provisions, and repair services to the fishing fleets and merchant vessels that operate in the region. The port handles approximately 4 million tonnes of cargo annually and operates a 24-hour emergency repair service for vessels damaged in typhoons. The {{nihongo|Oita Maritime Rescue Coordination Centre|大分海上救難調整センター|Oita Kaijō Kyūnan Chōsei Sentā}} coordinates search-and-rescue operations across a 500 km radius of the southeastern Shendan.

=== Ocean fishing ===
The Oita fishing fleet operates approximately 250 vessels, landing approximately 40,000 tonnes of seafood annually from the rich deep-water grounds of the southeastern Shendan. Key species include {{nihongo|bigeye tuna|メバチ|mebachi}}, {{nihongo|alfonsino|金眼鯛|kinmedai}}, and various deep-sea shrimp and crab species. The {{nihongo|Oita Tuna|大分鮪|Oita Maguro}} is prized for its high fat content, a product of the cold, deep waters in which it is caught.

=== Volcanic agriculture ===
[[File:Oita Kabosu Citrus.jpg|thumb|right|250px|Oita kabosu, a GI-protected sour citrus fruit unique to the prefecture]]
The volcanic soils of the main island support a distinctive agriculture, including {{nihongo|shiitake|椎茸}} mushroom cultivation on the volcanic slopes, {{nihongo|''kabosu''|臭橙}} (a sour citrus fruit unique to Oita), and {{nihongo|Oita barley|大分麦|Oita Mugi}} used in the local shochu distilling tradition. The {{nihongo|Oita Kabosu|大分臭橙|Oita Kabosu}} is a GI-protected product, and the citrus is used in sauces, beverages, and as a garnish for the prefecture's seafood dishes.
Oita's economy is driven by specialized small-craft shipbuilding and traditional bamboo joinery. Local boatyards construct aluminum-hull search-and-rescue craft, high-speed pilot vessels, and harbor tugs that service busy shipping channels throughout Yagikoshu. In rural districts, artisan cooperatives harvest giant madake bamboo, weaving high-tensile architectural screens, lightweight agricultural baskets, and delicate household furnishings exported across Adonia.

== Transportation ==

=== Air ===
[[Oita Airport]] (IATA: OIT) operates flights to [[Okami]], [[Toyozawa]], and [[Kii]], with seasonal services to [[Sakai]]. The airport is the primary gateway for visitors and essential for the transport of fresh seafood to the mainland markets.

=== Sea ===
The {{nihongo|Oita Ferry|大分フェリー|Oita Ferī}} operates services to [[Kii]] (8 hours) and [[Mutsu]] (10 hours), with car ferry services for inter-island transport. The {{nihongo|Oita Inter-Island Ferry|大分離島フェリー|Oita Ritō Ferī}} connects the smaller islands to the main island.

== Culture ==

=== Cuisine ===
Oita's cuisine is defined by the ocean and the volcano. The prefecture's signature dish is {{nihongo|''Oita maguro-zukuri''|大分鮪造り}}—a multi-course preparation of Oita bigeye tuna, served with {{nihongo|kabosu|臭橙}} juice instead of the usual soy sauce. Other specialities include {{nihongo|''shiitake donburi''|椎茸丼}} (mushroom rice bowl), {{nihongo|''Oita shochu''|大分焼酎|Oita Shōchū}} (barley shochu distilled from Oita barley), and {{nihongo|''tako-meshi''|タコ飯}} (octopus rice).

=== Festivals ===
* {{nihongo|'''Oita Maritime Festival'''|大分海祭り|Oita Umi Matsuri}} — Annual celebration of the shipbuilding and fishing industries (May)
* {{nihongo|'''Kabosu Festival'''|臭橙祭り|Kabosu Matsuri}} — Citrus harvest festival (October)
* {{nihongo|'''Volcano Festival'''|火山祭り|Kazan Matsuri}} — Annual commemoration of the 1783 Great Oita Eruption (August)

